# Dependency Intelligence Suite

> **Consolidation note.** This file merges five capabilities that are
> otherwise independent playbooks: codegraph substrate, package transitive
> mapping, code hierarchy mapping, .NET OSS remediation, Gradle transitive
> remediation. This trades the one-capability-per-file convention for a
> single entry point. Each Part keeps its own certification harness,
> Fidelity Ledger, and limitations section — consolidation means one file,
> not one undifferentiated process. Parts 2–5 do **not** require Part 1;
> `codegraph.json` is an accelerator for them, never a prerequisite.

## Part 0 — Routing

| Question | Go to |
|---|---|
| Build/refresh the repo knowledge graph; define agent tool calls | Part 1 |
| What packages does this repo pull in? Why is package X here? | Part 2 |
| What does this file/class depend on? What breaks if I change it? | Part 3 |
| Fix vulnerable/deprecated/outdated NuGet packages | Part 4 |
| Fix a Gradle transitive version that resolves wrong | Part 5 |
| Combined limitations, absence notation, command reference | Part 6 |

