# PART 6 — Cross-Cutting Reference

## 6.1 Explicit Absence Notation (all Parts)

- `Not detected — [what was scanned]`
- `Not run — resolver unavailable: [tool] not found on PATH`
- `Not applicable — [layer/tier] has no prerequisite artifacts in this repo`
- `Not verifiable — codegraph freshness unconfirmed: [reason]`
- `Degraded — [language] parsed by fallback scan, edges tagged INFERRED`
- `Not run — audit source unreachable: [source]. Absence of findings is NOT evidence of absence of vulnerabilities.`
- `Unremediated — [package]: no patched version published as of [date]`
- `Suppressed — [advisory], owner [x], review by [date]`
- `Override did not take — resolution reason still names [source] after change`

## 6.2 Combined Command Reference

| Ecosystem/Language | Package forward | Package reverse | Code forward | Code reverse |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| npm | `npm ls --all --json` | `npm explain <pkg>` | `madge <entry>` | `dependency-cruiser --reaches` |
| yarn | `yarn list --json` | `yarn why <pkg>` | — | — |
| pnpm | `pnpm list --depth Infinity --json` | `pnpm why <pkg>` | — | — |
| pip | `pipdeptree --json-tree` | `pipdeptree --reverse --packages <pkg>` | `pydeps <module>` | `grimp find_upstream_modules` |
| poetry | `poetry show --tree` | `poetry show --why <pkg>` | — | — |
| Maven | `mvn dependency:tree -Dverbose` | `mvn dependency:tree -Dincludes=<pkg>` | `jdeps -summary` | invert `jdeps` edges |
| Gradle | `./gradlew <mod>:dependencies` | `./gradlew <mod>:dependencyInsight --dependency <pkg>` | `jdeps -summary` | invert `jdeps` edges |
| NuGet | `dotnet list package --include-transitive` | `dotnet nuget why <pkg>` | Roslyn forward walk | `SymbolFinder.FindReferencesAsync` |
| Cargo | `cargo tree` | `cargo tree -i <pkg>` | `cargo modules generate graph` | invert generated graph |
| Go | `go mod graph` | `go mod why -m <module>` | `importgraph.Build().Forward` | `importgraph.Build().Reverse` |

## 6.3 Universal Principles (apply to every Part)

1. **Single authority per domain**, with rejected alternatives documented
   in that Part's Fidelity Ledger.
2. **Harness before work.** No Part proceeds past its Phase 0 gate.
3. **Evidence only.** Every finding cites a file path and the exact
   command that produced it. `INFERRED` is never presented as fact.
4. **Explicit absence.** Silence is never an answer; use §6.1 notation.
5. **Verify, don't assume.** A remediation is complete only when
   re-detection confirms it (Parts 4 and 5 verification gates).
6. **Separate scopes and break types.** dev vs runtime packages;
   compile-time vs runtime vs silent-data consumers. Never merged.
